[h1]ZeD UI [B42][/h1]
Every window, the HUD and the menus, rebuilt from scratch for Build 42. It looks like a Mac from 1993 because that's the computer we wanted to survive the apocalypse on. It plays with a controller as well as with a mouse and keys.

It's big, and it's new. Read the next bit before you subscribe.

[h2]Before you subscribe[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only.[/b] Built and tested on 42.21. It won't run on Build 41.
[*][b]Single player is where it's been tested.[/b] Multiplayer hasn't been. If you try it on a server, tell us how it went.
[*][b]It replaces vanilla's windows.[/b] Mods that add their own buttons to vanilla's inventory or character window won't show those buttons, because those windows are hidden. Mods that use the game's own systems (context menu options, container buttons, items, recipes) work. See the compatibility thread.
[*][b]It adds one item:[/b] a steel digital watch in the loot. Take ZeD off mid-save and those watches go with it. Everything else is interface, and safe to add or remove.
[*][b]English only for now.[/b] Translation support is the next big job. See the translations thread if you want to help.
[/list]

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[b]Your window and the world's window.[/b] Your stuff on one side: loot, what you wear, health, temperature, who you are, your journal, skills, the radio you carry. The world on the other: loot, crafting (at any bench or station near you), building, maps, foraging, animals, the radio nearby, the vehicle you're next to, furniture.

[b]Cards for everything.[/b] Click an item, a generator, a campfire, a farm plot, a trough, a padlock, a liquid: you get one card with what it is, what you can do and why you can't yet.

[b]The HUD.[/b] Your hands and hotbar on a belt. A watch you actually use. A dashboard when you drive. Moodles where you want them. A bar over your head that says what you're doing and how long the queue is (or just ten little lights, if you'd rather).

[b]The menus.[/b] The main menu is a desk with a CRT on it. Load, new game, mods, options, sandbox, character creation, server settings: all ZeD windows on that screen, with the game's own logic underneath.

[b]Controller.[/b] Everything you can do with a mouse, you can do with a pad. D-pad moves between things, A and B are left and right click, X and Y open things.

[b]Your colours.[/b] Dark, light or high contrast, nine accents, two text sizes, a UI scale for big screens.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]Main menu, Mods: turn on [b]ZeD UI[/b]. Put it after other interface mods in the load order.
[*]Start or continue a game.
[*]Options, Mods, ZeD UI: pick your theme, accent, text size, scale, where the moodles sit and how much the action bar says.
[*]Your inventory key opens your window. Your loot key opens the world's. On a controller, the same buttons as vanilla.
[/olist]
Big screen (1440p, 4K)? Leave UI scale on Auto, or set it yourself in the same place.

[h2]Something broke[/h2]
Post in the [b]Bug reports[/b] thread, not the comments. Comments scroll away, threads don't. Tell us:
[list]
[*]Your game version and ZeD's (the desk's ZeD menu, About).
[*]Your mod list.
[*]What you did, what you expected, what happened.
[*]Your console.txt: [i]C:\Users\(you)\Zomboid\console.txt[/i]. Put it on a paste site and post the link.
[/list]
Screenshots help more than words.

[h2]Requests, add-ons and translations[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Ideas and requests:[/b] the Requests thread. We read all of it, we can't build all of it.
[*][b]Making an add-on:[/b] the Add-on makers thread has the guides. Watches can be added today; tabs and themes are coming.
[*][b]Translating:[/b] the Translations thread. You'll only need text files, no fonts.
[/list]

[h2]Works with, and doesn't[/h2]
The compatibility thread keeps the list. Your own setup can be checked from the desk: Mods shows clashes between mods (two mods changing the same file, the same item or recipe) and tells you which one wins. Other mods that replace the whole interface won't mix with this one.

[h2]For server admins[/h2]
Workshop ID: (after the first upload)
Mod ID: ZeD_UI
[code]WorkshopItems=(Workshop ID)
Mods=ZeD_UI\[/code]
Every player needs it, since it adds an item.

